Step 1 — Create the Azure Files share

Portal: your Storage Account → File shares (left menu, under Data storage) → + File share
- Name: otc-uploads-files (any name — file shares and blob containers are separate namespaces, so it doesn't need to match the blob container name)
- Tier: Transaction optimized (default is fine for this)
- Click Create

Step 2 — Copy the same documents into the new share

Easiest if you already have the files locally (you can download them from the otc-uploads blob container first if needed: Storage Account → Containers → otc-uploads → select file → Download).

Via Portal (simplest, few files): open the new file share → + Add directory → create CASE123, then samples, then drag-and-drop the matching files into each, using the exact same filenames as in Blob (INFORMATION MEMORANDUM.docx, FINANCIAL MODEL.xlsx, Good Deal Guide.docx, BLANK OTC TEMPLATE.docx).

Via CLI, if you prefer (needs the storage account key — grab it from Storage Account → Access keys → key1, same one you already used for the mount):
$key = "<storage-account-key>"
az storage directory create --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --name CASE123 --account-key $key
az storage directory create --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --name samples --account-key $key

az storage file upload --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --source "CASE123\INFORMATION MEMORANDUM.docx" --path "CASE123/INFORMATION MEMORANDUM.docx" --account-key $key
az storage file upload --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --source "CASE123\FINANCIAL MODEL.xlsx" --path "CASE123/FINANCIAL MODEL.xlsx" --account-key $key
az storage file upload --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --source "CASE123\Good Deal Guide.docx" --path "CASE123/Good Deal Guide.docx" --account-key $key
az storage file upload --account-name <account> --share-name otc-uploads-files --source "samples\BLANK OTC TEMPLATE.docx" --path "samples/BLANK OTC TEMPLATE.docx" --account-key $key

Step 3 — Switch the existing Storage Mount to point at the new share

App Service → Configuration → Path mappings → open your existing Storage Mount entry (the one currently pointing at Blob container otc-uploads) and edit it:
- Storage type: change from "Azure Blob Container" to Azure Files
- Storage container/share: otc-uploads-files (the new share, not the old blob container)
- Access key: same key as before
- Mount path: /otc-uploads — leave this exactly as-is, unchanged

Click OK, then Save at the top.

Step 4 — Restart

App Service → Overview → Restart. Mount changes require a restart to actually reattach.
